<section id="connection" class="connection-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">02 / THE SHARED SERVICE</p><p class="section-note">Configure once. Connect every client.</p></div><div class="connection-intro"><h2>The connection<br>behind everything.</h2><div><p>One service connects your Amiga apps to Home Assistant. Apps share device states and controls. Your token stays in the bridge.</p></div></div><div class="protocol-diagram" aria-label="Home Assistant connects to the AmiHASS service using HTTPS REST. Amiga applications connect using Exec message ports and the C SDK. Scripts use the AMIHASS ARexx port."><div class="protocol-node"><span class="node-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span><strong>Home Assistant</strong><small>YOUR SERVER</small></div><div class="protocol-line"><small>HTTPS / REST</small><span>←────────→</span></div><div class="protocol-node bridge-node"><strong>AmiHASS</strong><small>ONE SHARED SERVICE</small></div><div class="protocol-line"><small>EXEC PORTS + ARexx</small><span>←────────→</span></div><div class="protocol-clients"><span>Dashboard + Browser</span><a class="novadock-trigger" href="#novadock-info">NovaDock <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a><span>Your apps / C SDK</span><span>Scripts / AMIHASS port</span></div></div><div class="service-notes"><p><strong>Work at Amiga speed.</strong> The bridge updates selected devices and shares results between apps. Low memory mode frees unused libraries while idle.</p><p><strong>Know what’s connected.</strong> See service, network and server status at a glance. Automatic reconnect helps recover from connection problems.</p></div></div></section>

<section id="downloads" class="section downloads-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">03 / DOWNLOADS</p></div><div class="download-intro"><h2>Bring it to<br>your Workbench.</h2><p>Includes the bridge, Preferences, Device Browser and Dashboard. The SDK is available separately below.</p></div><div class="release-meta"><span>AmigaOS 3.x</span><span>68000 or better</span><span>Free · MIT licensed</span></div><div id="release-content"><?php ah_render_downloads($catalog); ?></div><div class="release-status-row"><p id="release-status" class="download-caption" role="status"><?= ah_html(ah_release_status($catalog)) ?></p></div><details class="setup-details"><summary>Installation &amp; requirements <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="install-columns"><div><h3>From archive to Workbench.</h3><ol><li>Unpack the archive with its .info files.</li><li>Run <strong>Install</strong>. The final page lists installed locations.</li><li>Choose to open Preferences after a fresh install, or open <strong>AmiHASSPrefs</strong> in SYS:Prefs.</li><li>Choose Sample data or enter your server and token. Save, then Start.</li></ol><p>Browser and Dashboard normally install in SYS:Utilities. Updates preserve the service state. Uninstall can keep your settings.</p></div><div><h3>What you need.</h3><p>Use Installer 42+ and a screen of at least 640×256. Sample data works offline. Server data needs TCP/IP, <strong>C:curl</strong>, a token and HTTPS support—normally <strong>AmiSSL</strong>, certificates and a correct clock. AmiSSL needs a 68020+; check curl’s requirements too.</p><h3>Set up HTTPS first.</h3><ol><li>Download the AmigaOS 3 / m68k <a href="https://github.com/jens-maus/amissl/releases">AmiSSL runtime</a> and run its Install script.</li><li>Get a Classic m68k curl build from <a href="https://aminet.net/search?query=curl">Aminet</a> or <a href="https://curl.se/download.html">curl downloads</a>. Follow its instructions and install it as C:curl. AmigaOS 4 / PPC builds will not work.</li><li>Run <code>C:curl --version</code> to check HTTPS support. Set the clock and follow the package’s <a href="https://curl.se/docs/sslcerts.html">certificate instructions</a>.</li><li>Enter your URL and token in Server Settings, then Test connection. Check server logs if it fails.</li></ol><p>curl and AmiSSL are separate downloads. See the <a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/amihass/blob/main/REQUIREMENTS.txt">full installation guide</a> for details.</p><p>Download the matching checksum file and verify the archive:</p><pre><code id="checksum-command"><?= ah_html(ah_checksum_command($latest)) ?></code></pre><p>A matching archive reports <strong>OK</strong>.</p></div></div></details></div></section>
<section id="developers" class="section wrap developer-section"><div class="section-top"><p class="eyebrow">04 / FOR DEVELOPERS</p><p class="section-note">Build on the same connection.</p></div><div class="developer-grid"><div><h2>Your idea.<br>Our bridge.</h2><p class="developer-intro">Use the C SDK for native apps or ARexx for scripts. Browse devices, read states and send controls through the shared bridge.</p><div id="sdk-release-content" class="sdk-download"><?php ah_render_sdk($catalog); ?></div><div class="developer-links"><a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/amihass/tree/main/SDK">SDK guide ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/amihass/blob/main/SDK/example.c">Example client ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/amihass/tree/main/ARexx">ARexx scripts ↗</a></div></div></div></section>

